# state/ is NO LONGER ignored (#63): the paper ledger is now written by the
# paper-engine GitHub Action and committed, which is what makes the cloud the single
# owner. Logs stay local -- they are noise, not ledger.
state/logs/
*.egg-info/
build/
graphify-out/
.env
.env.*

# iCloud conflict copies. This repo lives in ~/Documents with Desktop & Documents sync
# on, and iCloud silently creates byte-identical "<name> 2.<ext>" duplicates. One got
# committed as a second paper-engine workflow and GitHub ran BOTH on every schedule.
# See the CI guard in tests.yml -- ignoring them is not enough on its own, because
# `git add -f` and some tools bypass it.
* 2.*
* 3.*
